# Published archive keeps only lib/, example/, doc/, skills/, README.md,
# CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE, and pubspec.yaml. Everything below is dev/CI/test
# tooling that must not ship to pub.dev.
#
# EVERY DIRECTORY PATTERN IS ROOT-ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, deliberately.
# .pubignore uses gitignore semantics, where a bare `config/` matches a directory
# named `config` at ANY DEPTH — including `lib/src/config/`. That is not a
# hypothetical: the inherited unanchored list is why BOTH earlier published
# diene_auth_engine releases (1.0.0 and 1.0.1) are structurally unusable. Their
# `lib/src/config/auth_engine_config.dart` was silently dropped from the archive
# while `lib/diene_auth_engine.dart` still `export`ed it, so any consumer that
# touched the barrel failed to compile.
#
# THIS PACKAGE'S STATUS, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED: no directory under `lib/`
# currently matches any pattern in this list, so the defect was LATENT here, not
# live — this file was inherited unanchored from the dart-lib scaffolding and is
# anchored here before any publish. Latent is untriggered, not safe: this package
# ships `lib/src/stub/` and `lib/src/journey/`, and a future `lib/src/test/` or
# `lib/src/tool/` would vanish from the archive silently. Anchoring makes these
# exclusions mean what they were written to mean.
#
# The durable control is NOT this file being read correctly — it is
# scripts/validate/publish-archive.sh, which asserts every tracked `lib/` Dart
# source actually reaches the `pub publish --dry-run` file list and every
# relative barrel export resolves and ships.
/.claude/
/.dart_tool/
/.direnv/
/.github/
/.kagent/
/.kloop/
/config/
/contracts/
/coverage/
/docs/
/nix/
/probes/
/scripts/
/tasks/
/test/
/tool/
/.coderabbit.yaml
/.envrc
/.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc
/.markdownlint.json
/.prettierignore
/.prettierrc.yaml
/atomi_release.yaml
/codecov.yml
/flake.lock
/flake.nix
/lpsm.yaml
/Taskfile.yaml
/CLAUDE.md
/VERSION
